('Brazoria', 'offered', 'Split Payment/Half Pay . Pay half of your property taxes by November 30th and the remaining half no later than June 30th of the following year without accruing any penalty and interest.', 'https://www.brazoriacountytx.gov/departments/tax-office/property-taxes/payment-options', '{"quarter":{"url":"https://www.brazoriacountytx.gov/departments/tax-office/property-taxes/payment-options","quote":"Over 65/Disabled/Disabled Veteran Installment Plan ."},"partial":{"url":"https://www.brazoriacountytx.gov/departments/tax-office/property-taxes/payment-options","quote":"If you are unable to pay the total amount of your taxes due in full, the Brazoria County Tax Office accepts partial payments in any amount."}}'::jsonb, '2026-11-05'::date),
('Brazos', 'offered', 'Brazos County taxing jurisdictions offer the two part payment plan to their taxpayers allowing a payment of ½ of the property tax bill on or before November 30 of the year the taxes are billed, and the second half payment on or before June 30 of the following year. (Local news report; the tax office''s own site, brazostax.org, didn''t state it.)', 'https://wtaw.com/deadline-reminders-for-brazos-county-property-owners-planning-to-make-split-payments/', '{"quarter":{"url":"https://comptroller.texas.gov/taxes/property-tax/pay/index.php","quote":"You may have the option to set up an installment plan."}}'::jsonb, '2026-11-05'::date),
